ce the understanding and application of clinical nutrition in various healthcare settings.", "CLINICAL PATHOLOGY:", "SOCIETY FOR ADOLESCENT HEALTH AND MEDICINE:The Society for Adolescent Health and Medicine is an organization focused on the health and medical management of adolescents, particularly concerning eating disorders.", "ISABEL M. CORNEJO-PAREJA:Isabel M. Cornejo-Pareja is a researcher and author associated with the study of intestinal microbiota and obesity.", "ARACELI MUÑOZ-GARACH:Araceli Muñoz-Garach is a researcher and author involved in the field of endocrinology and nutrition.", "FRANCISCO J. TINAHONES-MADUEÑO:Francisco J. Tinahones-Madueño is a researcher and author specializing in endocrinology and nutrition.", "J ADOLESCENT HEALTH:J Adolescent Health is a medical journal that publishes research and articles related to adolescent health issues, including eating disorders.", "RESTRICTIVE EATING DISORDERS:", "PROYECTO DEL MICROBIOMA HUMANO:El Proyecto del Microbioma Humano es una iniciativa de investigación a gran escala que estudia la diversidad y funcionalidad de la microbiota intestinal humana.", "META HIT:MetaHIT es un proyecto de investigación que se centra en la caracterización de la microbiota intestinal y su relación con la salud humana.", "LACTOBACILLUS:Lactobacillus is a genus of bacteria that resides in the gastrointestinal tract and is widely recognized for its numerous health benefits, particularly in relation to digestive health. This genus is commonly utilized as probiotics, which are live microorganisms that confer health advantages when consumed in adequate amounts. Lactobacillus is known for its ability to ferment lactose and produce lactic acid, contributing to gut health and the maintenance of a positive metabolic profile.\n\nResearch has indicated that Lactobacillus may have beneficial effects on obesity and metabolic health, making it a subject of interest in studies related to these areas. Additionally, Lactobacillus can ferment undigested carbohydrates into D-lactic acid, which may lead to complications in certain patients, such as those with short bowel syndrome (SIC). The growth and activity of Lactobacillus can be enhanced by prebiotic fibers, further supporting its role in promoting gut health.\n\nOverall, Lactobacillus is a significant type of beneficial bacteria within the phylum Firmicutes, playing a crucial role in fermentation processes and contributing positively to digestive and metabolic health.", "STREPTOCOCCUS:Streptococcus is a genus of bacteria belonging to the phylum Firmicutes. These bacteria are commonly found in the gastrointestinal tract and play a significant role in human health and microbiota. Streptococcus can have both beneficial and pathogenic effects, highlighting its dual nature in the context of human health."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}